# The extension reads the repo root .env — there is normally no extension/.env at all.
# vite.config.ts maps the root's backend-named keys onto the VITE_ names the source
# uses: SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_KEY and API_BASE. Only those three cross over; the rest
# of the root .env (Nemotron key, database password) never reaches the bundle.
#
# Create an extension/.env only to override the root for your own machine. Anything set
# here wins. The Supabase URL and anon key are project identifiers rather than secrets,
# so they ship inside the bundle by design (see docs/architecture.md section 7).

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Backend base URL, including the scheme.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000
